<title>USA: U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to watch - May 14.</title>
<headline>U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to watch - May 14.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stocks to watch this morning:</p>
<p>* Compaq Computer Corp to add 2,000 sales jobs -- Wall Street Journal.</p>
<p>* Monsanto and a unit of Rhone-Poulenc SA sign an agreement for the future marketing in the United States of some pre-mixed corn herbicide products.</p>
<p>* Hughes Supply Inc reports first quarter earnings per share of $0.66, up from $0.63 a year earlier.  </p>
<p>* Republic Industries Inc to triple authorized common shares, list on New York Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>* Tiffany &amp; Co first quarter earnings rise.</p>
<p>* Deutsche Lufthansa AG announces partnership efforts among a group of leading airlines.</p>
<p>((--Wall Street Desk (212) 859-1730))</p>
